course: dictionary
lesson: 15204
title: Half and partly: the prefix semi-
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Semi- is a prefix, a small part added to the front of a word. It means half, or partly. «Mia drew a semicircle on the paper.» Semicircle is made of semi- and circle, so a semicircle is half a circle.
explain: Semi- can help you work out new words. «We are through to the semi-final!» Semi-final is the round just before the final. If you know semi- means half or partly, you can guess the semi-final is not the big final yet.
explain: Sometimes semi is a short word on its own. «They live in a semi on Elm Street.» In the UK, a semi is a semi-detached house, joined to one other house. In the US, a semi can mean a large lorry, so look at the clues in the text to find the right meaning.
fact: Semi- is a prefix that means half or partly.
fact: «Semicircle» means half a circle.
fact: «Semi-final» means the round before the final in a sports competition.
fact: «Semi-detached» means a house joined to one other house on one side (UK, Ireland, Australia).
fact: In the US, Canada and Australia, informal «semi» can mean a very large lorry, a semi-trailer truck.
exercise: «Mia drew a semicircle.» What does semi- mean in semicircle? | Double | *Half, or partly | Very large | Round and whole
exercise: «We are through to the semis!» In sport, what is a semi? | *The round before the final | A practice game for fun | The very last match of the year | A referee's whistle
exercise: «They bought a semi in Leeds.» In the UK, what is a semi? | *A house joined to one other house | A large lorry | A type of milk | A semicolon
test: What does the prefix semi- mean? | Under water | *Half, or partly | Twice | Very large
test: In the UK, «a semi» is most likely to be what? | *A house joined to one other house | A tall tree | A kind of cake | A lorry carrying goods
exam: Which meaning fits «We won our semi-final on Friday»? | The final match of the year | *The round just before the final | A friendly practice game | A game played on a Sunday
